{"type":"runFinished","data":{"sessionId":"sess_9b3bf16a-3945-4b17-b19a-d7e3bc3c7e18","status":"success","stopReason":"end_turn","finalText":"I logged an `issues` verdict on W5 and added four open nodes to `.dfs/items/W5.md`. I changed no code, and the working tree outside `.dfs/` is as I found it.\n\n`test_web` passes (32 tests). Those tests only check the page source for wiring, and I couldn't render the page: the sandbox has no JS engine (I looked for node, deno, bun and quickjs). I traced `blocks()` by hand on sample text and found no wrong output beyond the numbering fault below. I found no stale docs or leftover scaffolding, and escaping runs before any rule, so file text can't become HTML.\n\n- **W5.4 (Fix, parent W5.2):** numbered lists always render from 1. `blocks()` throws away the source number, so a list interrupted by a paragraph restarts at 1, and \"see step 3\" can point at the wrong item.\n- **W5.5 (Hypothesis, parent W5.3):** lists are flat and every `#` heading becomes an `<h5>`. That narrows what \"render rich text\" shows, and the author might want nested lists and distinct heading levels.\n- **W5.6 (Hypothesis, parent W5.1):** single newlines inside a paragraph are now joined into one line, where the page used to keep them. A raise written one fact per line without bullets will run together.\n- **W5.7 (Minor findings):**\n  - The two new tests only grep the page source, so a wrong rule would not fail them.\n  - The page has never been rendered, so the author should look at it once.\n  - A `|` or `>` line in the middle of a paragraph starts a table or quote block, and the un-prefixed lines after a quote become a new paragraph. This isn't documented at `blocks()`.","finalTextTruncated":false}}

